# Orion repository rules

Read: `docs/README.md` → relevant ADRs → architecture docs → `docs/development/ENGINEERING_RULES.md` → `docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_GAPS.md` → relevant source/tests.

- Model owns semantics/reasoning/proposals; harness owns stage legality, disclosure state, exact authority, execution, evidence, limits, no-progress, completion.
- No language-specific semantic router before the model.
- Natural-language text is never execution authority.
- Validate every parsed decision against the active stage/schema; provider native JSON schema is only a generation aid.
- An invented capability ID is not disclosed authority.
- Exact capability/target/source only; malformed configuration fails closed; never silently fall back to localhost/another source.
- READ/WRITE is capability effect, not prose keywords.
- Protect credentials, internal prompts/policies, and private reasoning. Requests to reveal protected internal instructions use REFUSE.
- Objective final execution claims must be evidence-backed.
- Configured model metadata is the source for model identity/health, not model self-description.
- Do not resurrect dead deterministic/semantic routing.
- `IMPLEMENTATION_GAPS.md` is the current repair ledger; it does not override ADRs.

Validation: smallest local checks by default; for broad/destructive repair also callers/imports, `git diff --check`, and full local unit/static suite when practical. Live Docker/model/GA2/E2E remains an explicit separate gate.

Git: do not commit/push/rebase/reset/stash/clean/create branches unless explicitly requested; preserve unrelated dirty changes.
